WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
Then I went to a football game with Helen Gordon.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:13.060
And this later became quite an issue because when I was sitting up in Columbus [Mississippi],

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.640
I thought the . . . I mean the football tickets.

4
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.900
I thought, “Oh my goodness, I have to have football tickets!”

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:26.040
I’ve been in schools like Vanderbilt with football, Texas with football . . . but I was always given football tickets.

6
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.960
But you did not give anybody a ticket here.

7
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:37.240
And so I called up and said that I would like to have two football tickets and . . . That was later,

8
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.600
after I was appointed, of course.

9
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.560
I was talking to somebody, whoever was the business manager, and he said, well,

10
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.380
they would work it out and that the price would be so and so.

11
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.640
Well, I assumed that was the way it was done, so it was okay.

12
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.980
Well, this created the biggest to-do you’ve ever heard of because, they realized that I,

13
00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:06.800
as a new dean, had to have comparable tickets to the Dean of Men and to the outgoing dean.

14
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.320
But she was not going to give up her tickets.

15
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.560
I remember that.

16
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.220
So I now sit opposite, on the fifty-yard line,

17
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:24.540
the Dean of Men is on one side of the aisle on that between the . . . and then I’m over on the other side.

18
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.240
Those were not the seats, though, that I was given at first,

19
00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:35.160
but they . . . I was in the same section they were, and of course I wouldn’t have known to question it.

20
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:41.800
Well, anyhow, I went to the football game that afternoon, or that night, after that dinner in the Union.

21
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:49.600
And I remember that Helen Gordon and I went together.

22
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.400
Now I don’t know who normally went with her, but she did take me to the game,

23
00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:01.440
and Mrs. Long, the senator’s wife, was sitting in front.

24
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.200
Katherine Long.

25
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.720
Yeah, Katherine Long was in front.

26
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.760
I remember I met her,

27
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:13.600
and later we always when . . . as we’ve seen each other she always remembers that she saw me at that football game.
